G00000179832","entrez_id":["727957"],"uniprot":["Q8NDA8"],"ncbi_summary":null,"ncbi_source":null,"uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8NDA8","text":"Lysosome fission factor (PubMed:38538795). Recruited to lysosomes by RAB7 (RAB7A or RAB7B) at scission sites and homooligomerizes to mediate the constriction and scission of lysosomal tubules (PubMed:38538795). May sever membranes by inserting amphipathic helices into one bilayer leaflet (PubMed:38538795). Lysosome fission is required to maintain their steady-state number, shape, size, composition and function, and to accomplish regeneration (PubMed:38538795)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}